(Northwind Robotics Inc. - Annual Report 2025) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Letter from the Chief Executive Officer) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dear shareholders,) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2025 was the strongest year in Northwind's history. Northwind Robotics was founded in 2014) Tj T*
(in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, with a mission to build robots that work safely alongside) Tj T*
(people. Eleven years later our machines operate in hospitals, warehouses and farms around) Tj T*
(the world.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Total revenue for fiscal year 2025 was $412.6 million, compared with $338.2 million in) Tj T*
(fiscal year 2024. We ended the year with 1,870 full-time employees, up from 1,540 a year) Tj T*
(earlier.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The year was not without challenges. Shortages of motion-controller chips slowed Atlas) Tj T*
(deliveries in the first quarter, and higher freight costs weighed on margins in the summer.) Tj T*
(Our teams responded by redesigning two circuit boards and by moving more final assembly) Tj T*
(closer to customers. By the fourth quarter, delivery times had returned to normal.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(We also made important progress in healthcare. The Helix surgical platform began commercial) Tj T*
(sales in the United States, and the first hospitals reported shorter operating times for) Tj T*
(knee replacement procedures.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Our priorities for the coming year are disciplined growth, operational resilience and) Tj T*
(continued investment in research. I want to thank our customers, our partners and every) Tj T*
(member of the Northwind team for an exceptional year.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Dr. Elena Marsh) Tj T*
(Chief Executive Officer) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
