(Business Overview) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Northwind operates three business segments.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Warehouse Automation designs the Atlas family of autonomous mobile robots \(AMRs\) that move) Tj T*
(goods inside distribution centres. Atlas robots are sold together with a fleet-management) Tj T*
(software subscription called Atlas Control, which schedules missions, balances charging and) Tj T*
(reports utilisation to the customer.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Surgical Robotics develops the Helix platform, a robotic assistant for minimally invasive) Tj T*
(orthopaedic surgery. Helix systems are sold to hospitals with a multi-year service contract) Tj T*
(that covers maintenance, software updates and instrument supply.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Agricultural Robotics builds Furrow, a solar-powered weeding robot used by vegetable) Tj T*
(growers. Furrow uses cameras to tell crops from weeds and removes weeds mechanically,) Tj T*
(without herbicides.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Northwind serves customers in 23 countries. Our largest customer, Meridian Logistics,) Tj T*
(accounted for 14% of total revenue in 2025. No other customer accounted for more than 5% of) Tj T*
(revenue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Recurring revenue from software subscriptions and service contracts was $96.5 million in) Tj T*
(2025, or about 23% of total revenue, compared with $71.0 million in 2024.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
