(Risk Factors) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Supplier concentration: Northwind relies on a single supplier, Kestrel Semiconductors, for) Tj T*
(the motion-controller chips used in all Atlas and Helix robots. A disruption at Kestrel) Tj T*
(could delay production for several months. We are qualifying a second supplier, but this) Tj T*
(process is not expected to finish before 2027.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Customer concentration: Meridian Logistics represented 14% of 2025 revenue. The loss of) Tj T*
(Meridian, or a significant reduction in its orders, would materially reduce our revenue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Trade and tariffs: approximately 35% of our component costs are imported, and changes in) Tj T*
(tariffs could increase costs.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Cybersecurity: our fleet-management software connects robots to customer networks; a) Tj T*
(security breach could harm customers and our reputation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Regulation: Surgical Robotics products are subject to medical device regulation in every) Tj T*
(market where they are sold. Delays in approvals could postpone revenue.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Competition: larger industrial automation companies are entering the autonomous mobile robot) Tj T*
(market and may compete aggressively on price.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
